    "Friday Ziyarat of the Prophet and Imams\nOn Friday, do ghusl and put on clean clothes. Go out into the desert, or up onto your roof, and pray four units with any surahs you know. After the prayer, stand facing the qiblah and say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAN NABIYYU WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah’s mercy and blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ الْمُرْسَلُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAN NABIYYUL MURSAL\nPeace be upon you, O missioned Prophet,\nوَالْوَصِيُّ الْمُرْتَضٰى\nWAL WASIYYUL MURTADAA\nand (peace be upon you) O well-pleased successor (of the Prophet),\nوَالسَّيِّدَةُ الْكُبْرٰى وَالسَّيِّدَةُ الزَّهْرَاۤءُ\nWAS SAYYIDATUL KUBRAA WAS SAYYIDATUZ ZAHRAA'\nand (peace be upon you) O grand lady, and O Luminous lady,\nوَالسِّبْطَانِ الْمُنْتَجَبَانِ\nWAS SIBTAANIL MUNTAJABAAN\nand (peace be upon you) O two elite grandsons (of the Prophet),\nوَالْاَوْلَادُ الْاَعْلَامُ وَالْاُمَنَاۤءُ الْمُنْتَجَبُوْنَ\nWAL AWLAADUL A'LAAMU WAL UMANAA'UL MUNTAJABOON\nand (peace be upon you) O descendants, the elite signs and the well-selected trustees.\nجِئْتُ انْقِطَاعًا اِلَيْكُمْ وَاِلٰى اٰبَاۤئِكُمْ\nJI'TUN QITAA'AN ILAYKUM WA ILAA AABAA'IKUM\nHere I come, devoting myself to you and to your fathers,\nوَوَلَدِكُمُ الْخَلَفِ عَلٰى بَرَكَةِ الْحَقِّ\nWA WALADIKUMUL KHALAFI A'LAA BARAKATIL HAQQ\nand to your son, the Successor, on the blessing of the truth.\nفَقَلْبِيْ لَكُمْ مُسَلِّمٌ وَنُصْرَتِيْ لَكُمْ مُعَدَّةٌ\nFAQALBEE LAKUM MUSALLIMUN WA NUSRATEE LAKUM MU'ADDAH\nMy heart is thus subservient to you and my support is prepared for you\nحَتّٰى يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ بِدِيْنِهٖ\nHATTAA YAHKUMALLAAHU BIDEENIH\nuntil Allah will judge about His religion.\nفَمَعَكُمْ مَعَكُمْ لَا مَعَ عَدُوِّكُمْ\nFAMA'AKUM MA'AKUM LAA MA'A A'DUWWIKUM\nI am with you, verily with you, but not with your enemy.\nاِنِّي لَمِنَ الْقَاۤئِلِيْنَ بِفَضْلِكُمْ مُقِرٌّ بِرَجْعَتِكُمْ\nINNEE LAMINAL QAA'ILEENA BIFADLIKUM MUQIRRUN BIRAJ'ATIKUM\nI am one of them who believe in your superiority, and I acknowledge your Return.\nلَاۤ اُنْكِرُ لِلّٰهِ قُدْرَةً\nLAA UNKIRU LILLAAHI QUDRAH\nI never deny the all-powerfulness of Allah,\nوَلَاۤ اَزْعُمُ اِلَّا مَا شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ\nWA LAA AZ'UMU ILLAA MAA SHAA'ALLAAH\nand I do not claim but that which Allah wills.\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ ذِي الْمُلْكِ وَالْمَلَكُوْتِ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI DHIL MULKI WAL MALAKOOT\nGlory be to Allah, Lord of kingdom and realm.\nيُسَبِّحُ اللّٰهَ بِاَسْمَاۤئِهٖ جَمِيْعُ خَلْقِهٖ\nYUSABBIHULLAAHA BI-ASMAA'IHEE JAMEE'U KHALQIH\nAll His creatures glorify Allah by His Names.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلٰۤى اَرْوَاحِكُمْ وَاَجْسَادِكُمْ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAA ARWAAHIKUM WA AJSAADIKUM\nPeace be upon your souls and your bodies.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you all.",
    "Salawat of Imam Ali (a.s.)\n[Surah Al-Ahzab](A37), verse 56:\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ وَمَلَاۤئِكَتَهٗ يُصَلُّوْنَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ\nINNALLAAHA WA MALAA'IKATAHOO YUSALLOONA A'LAN NABIYY\n“Lo! Allah and His angels shower blessings on the Prophet.\nيَاۤ اَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا صَلُّوْا عَلَيْهِ وَسَلِّمُوْا تَسْلِيْمًا\nYAA AYYUHAL LADHEENA AAMANOO SALLOO A'LAYHI WA SALLIMOO TASLEEMAA\nO you who believe, ask blessings on him and salute him with a worthy salutation.”\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَبَارِكْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA BAARIK A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nsend benedictions upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَتَحَنَّنْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA TAHANNAN A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nhave compassion upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَسَلِّمْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA SALLIM A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nand send peace upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nكَاَفْضَلِ مَا صَلَّيْتَ وَبَارَكْتَ وَتَرَحَّمْتَ وَتَحَنَّنْتَ وَسَلَّمْتَ\nKA-AFDALI MAA SALLAYTA WA BAARAKTA WA TARAHHAMTA WA TAHANNANTA WA SALLAMT\nas the best of what You have sent of blessings, benedictions, mercy, compassion, and peace\nعَلٰۤى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاٰلِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ اِنَّكَ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ\nA'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALI IBRAAHEEMA INNAKA HAMEEDUN MAJEED\nupon (Prophet) Abraham and the Household of Abraham. You are verily Owner of praise, Owner of glory.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا الْوَسِيْلَةَ\nALLAAHUMMA A'TI MUHAMMADANIL WASEELAH\nO Allah, give Muhammad [the right of] mediation,\nوَالشَّرَفَ وَالْفَضِيْلَةَ وَالْمَنْزِلَةَ الْكَرِيْمَةَ\nWASH SHARAFA WAL FADEELATA WAL MANZILATAL KAREEMAH\nhonor, virtue, and noble rank.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'L MUHAMMADAN WA AALA MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, make Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nاَعْظَمَ الْخَلَاۤئِقِ كُلِّهِمْ شَرَفًا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ\nA'ZAMAL KHALAA'IQI KULLIHIM SHARAFAN YAWMAL QIYAAMAH\nthe most honored of all creatures on the Resurrection Day,\nوَاَقْرَبَهُمْ مِنْكَ مَقْعَدًا\nWA AQRABAHUM MINKA MAQ'ADAA\nthe closest to You in position,\nوَاَوْجَهَهُمْ عِنْدَكَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ جَاهًا\nWA AWJAHAHUM I'NDAKA YAWMAL QIYAAMATI JAAHAA\nthe most notable with You on the Resurrection Day,\nوَاَفْضَلَهُمْ عِنْدَكَ مَنْزِلَةً وَنَصِيْبًا\nWA AFDALAHUM I'NDAKA MANZILATAN WA NASEEBAA\nand the most favored with You in rank and share.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِ مُحَمَّدًا اَشْرَفَ الْمَقَامِ\nALLAAHUMMA A'TI MUHAMMADAN ASHRAFAL MAQAAM\nO Allah, give Muhammad the most honorable position,\nوَحِبَاۤءَ السَّلَامِ وَشَفَاعَةَ الْاِسْلَامِ\nWA HIBAA'AS SALAAMI WA SHAFAA'ATAL ISLAAM\nthe gift of peace, and the intercession of Islam.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاَلْحِقْنَا بِهٖ غَيْرَ خَزَايَا\nALLAAHUMMA WA ALHIQNAA BIHEE GHAYRA KHAZAAYAA\nO Allah, join us to him while we are neither disgraced,\nوَلَا نَاكِثِيْنَ وَلَا نَادِمِيْنَ وَلَا مُبَدِّلِيْنَ\nWA LAA NAAKITHEENA WA LAA NAADIMEENA WA LAA MUBADDILEEN\nnor violating, nor regretful, nor distorting.\nاِلٰهَ الْحَقِّ اٰمِيْنَ\nILAAHAL HAQQI AAMEEN\nO God of the Truth, respond to us."
  ],
  "merits": "Ziyarat from a distance: in Zad al-Ma'ad, among the acts of 17 Rabi al-Awwal, the birthday of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), Allamah al-Majlisi gives this ziyarat from Shaykh al-Mufid, al-Shahid and Sayyid Ibn Tawus, for one who wishes to visit the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) from anywhere other than Madinah. In Madinah itself, his ziyarat is [Method of Ziyarat of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in Madinah](AP2).\n\nFriday ziyarat: Shaykh al-Tusi in Misbah al-Mutahajjid and Sayyid Ibn Tawus in Jamal al-Usbu', among the acts of Friday, say it is recommended to visit the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and the Imams (a.s.) on Fridays. Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that one who is far away and wishes to visit the tombs of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), Amir al-Mu'minin, Lady Fatimah al-Zahra, Imam al-Hasan, Imam al-Husayn and the other Imams (a.s.) should do ghusl on Friday, put on two clean garments and go out into the desert (or, in another narration, up onto his roof), pray four units with any surah he can recite, and then stand facing the qiblah and say this ziyarat.\n\nSalawat of Imam Ali: Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) recited this invocation of blessings upon the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in one of his Friday sermons, as al-Rawdah min al-Kafi records. It opens with the verse of [Surah Al-Ahzab](A37), 33:56.\n\nGreeting the Prophet from afar: according to many narrations, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is told of the greetings and the blessings of everyone who greets him or invokes blessings upon him, wherever they are. One hadith says an angel is appointed to answer everyone who says, “May Allah bless Muhammad and his Household and grant them peace,” with “And upon you too.” The angel then tells the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that so-and-so has greeted him, and he answers, “And peace be upon him too.”\n\nIn a reliable narration, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, “He who visits my tomb after my death is as one who emigrated to me in my lifetime. If you cannot visit my tomb, send me your greetings, for they reach me.” Many other narrations carry the same meaning.\n\nOther forms: Shaykh Abbas al-Qummi also points to the two forms of ziyarat of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) for Saturday, in [Ziyarat on Saturday](K3), to be recited for their reward. Another invocation of blessings upon him and his Household, from Imam al-Hasan al-Askari (a.s.), is [Salawat upon the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)](E128)."
